<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<chapter xml:id="chapter-linear-models" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Linear Models</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>
      This chapter is the fulcrum between the two pieces of
      statistics: descriptive and inference. Inference statistics
      tries to do more than just disply a data set: it tries, instead,
      to tease out some conclusions from the data set. There is a huge
      variety of these possible conclusions. In these two outcomes,
      we're start with the conclusion of a linear relationship between
      two numeric variables. Such a relation is called a linear model. 
    </p>
  </introduction>

  <xi:include href="clo9-linear-regression.ptx" />
  <xi:include href="clo10-linear-analysis.ptx" />

</chapter>
